[{"category":"section","location":"#Liblevenshtein.jl","page":"API and usage","text":"Liblevenshtein provides Unicode edit-distance functions and lazy, snapshot-consistent fuzzy search over any negotiated Vinary Tree dictionary provider. Its Julia API preserves byte, Unicode-scalar, and unsigned-token domains through multiple dispatch.","title":"Liblevenshtein.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Common-usage","page":"API and usage","text":"using Liblevenshtein\n\ndistance(\"kitten\", \"sitting\")\ndistance(\"kitten\", \"sitting\"; threshold=2)\noptimal_string_alignment_distance(\"ab\", \"ba\")\ntrue_damerau_distance(\"CA\", \"ABC\")\nmerge_and_split_distance(\"m\", \"rn\")\ndistance(UInt8[0xff, 0x00], UInt8[0xff, 0x01])\ndistance(UInt64[10, 20], UInt64[20, 10])\n\nAll four distance families use the same multiple-dispatch contract. Strings count Unicode scalar values, AbstractVector{UInt8} values are arbitrary binary data, and AbstractVector{UInt64} values are application tokens. Supplying threshold=k returns the exact result when it is at most k and nothing otherwise. Dense vectors cross the native boundary without a copy; non-dense abstract vectors are materialized temporarily to satisfy C's contiguous-buffer contract.\n\nThe repository's domain-preserving distance design explains the shared recurrences, ABI names, threshold sentinels, and generated differential tests.","title":"Common usage"},{"category":"section","location":"#Resource-backed-search","page":"API and usage","text":"A Transducer accepts a VinaryTreeInterop.Resource or VinaryTreeInterop.Dictionary. Reuse it across queries and close it deterministically:\n\ntransducer = Transducer(dictionary, ALGORITHM_STANDARD)\ntry\n    for match in query(transducer, \"speling\", 2)\n        println(match.term, \" \", match.distance)\n    end\nfinally\n    close(transducer)\nend\n\nUse reduce_batches! when matches do not need to escape the callback. Each BorrowedMatch expires when its callback returns; call materialize inside the callback when an independently owned value is required.","title":"Resource-backed search"},{"category":"section","location":"#Runtime-edit-grammars-and-standalone-automata","page":"API and usage","text":"GeneralizedAutomaton executes an immutable runtime operation set. The native engine converts accepted decimal weights to one exact scale, and Julia exposes an accepted cost as Rational{Int}:\n\noperations = GeneralizedOperationSet(\n    GeneralizedOperation(0, 1, 1, :insert),\n    GeneralizedOperation(1, 0, 1, :delete),\n    GeneralizedOperation(1, 1, 0, :equal;\n        applicability=APPLICABILITY_EQUAL),\n    GeneralizedOperation(1, 1, 0.5, :substitute),\n)\n\nautomaton = GeneralizedAutomaton(2, operations)\ntry\n    @assert evaluate(automaton, \"cat\", \"cut\").distance == 1 // 2\nfinally\n    close(automaton)\nend\n\nUniversalAutomaton selects the standard, adjacent-transposition, or merge-and-split specialization. Input types select byte, Unicode-scalar, or u64-token semantics. A UniversalPolicy owns typed directional zero-cost equivalences; the default UNRESTRICTED_POLICY avoids policy allocation and lookup.\n\npolicy = UniversalPolicy('p' => 'f')\nautomaton = UniversalAutomaton(0, policy)\ntry\n    @assert accepts(automaton, \"p\", \"f\")\n    @assert !accepts(automaton, \"f\", \"p\")\nfinally\n    close(automaton)\nend\n\nCall online plus advance! for a long-lived prefix state, or use the closeable prefix_observations iterator for a finite target. Its do-block form closes on early return as well as ordinary exhaustion. AutomatonLimits supplies explicit native source, target, retained-cell, and per-step work ceilings; a failed advance leaves the prior observation committed.\n\nThe initial observation describes the empty target. Each successful advance! commits one domain unit and yields the same value as a subsequent observation; prefix_observations yields only post-advance values, so an empty target yields no iterator items. A complete evaluate agrees with the last prefix value, or with the initial value for an empty target. Generalized scaled_distance is a within-budget numerator over scale_denominator, not an approximate float; absence means the full source is not within budget at that prefix. Closing a parent configuration does not invalidate its bound online state. Online states are exclusive and must be explicitly closed when stopping early.\n\nGeneralized current-row emptiness is not a pruning certificate: a multi-target operation can revive from an older retained row. Universal alive == false, by contrast, is permanent. Standalone automata compare one source/target pair; dictionary-product traversal remains a distinct bounded native capability. The Julia package guide records the independent public-Rust differential corpus, measured scenarios, and CI regression budgets. Dictionary-product traversal is owned by a separate Julia query-capability task, not by this standalone qualification.","title":"Runtime edit grammars and standalone automata"},{"category":"section","location":"#Bounded-repeated-query-caching","page":"API and usage","text":"QueryCache is an opt-in complete-result memo for repeated workloads. It uses the native TinyLFU-admission/SIEVE-eviction implementation rather than a Julia dictionary, preserves hard per-order entry and logical-weight bounds, and invalidates residency when the provider revision changes:\n\ncache = QueryCache(transducer; max_entries=512, max_weight=32 * 1024 * 1024)\ntry\n    matches = collect(query(cache, \"speling\", 2))\n    @show cache_stats(cache)\nfinally\n    close(cache)\nend\n\nThe cache is mutable, exclusive, and lock-free by ownership convention. Shard one cache per task or worker for parallel use. A miss returns the exact result even when policy rejects it; approximation affects only which reusable entries remain resident. Providers without stable snapshot identity are rejected because correctness takes precedence over hit rate.","title":"Bounded repeated-query caching"},{"category":"section","location":"#Automata","page":"API and usage","text":"Transducer accepts ALGORITHM_STANDARD, ALGORITHM_TRANSPOSITION, ALGORITHM_MERGE_AND_SPLIT, or ALGORITHM_DAMERAU_LEVENSHTEIN. Standard, merge-and-split, and unrestricted Damerau-Levenshtein are metrics. The optimal-string-alignment transposition variant is intentionally non-metric and does not compose repeated edits through the same substring.","title":"Automata"},{"category":"section","location":"#API","page":"API and usage","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"constant","location":"#Liblevenshtein.ABI_VERSION","page":"API and usage","text":"Stable liblevenshtein native ABI generation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.ABI_VERSION"},{"category":"constant","location":"#Liblevenshtein.API_REVISION","page":"API and usage","text":"Minimum additive native API revision required by this facade.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.API_REVISION"},{"category":"constant","location":"#Liblevenshtein.BUILD_FEATURE_CORE","page":"API and usage","text":"Compiled native feature bit: core.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.BUILD_FEATURE_CORE"},{"category":"constant","location":"#Liblevenshtein.BUILD_FEATURE_PHONETIC","page":"API and usage","text":"Compiled native feature bit: phonetic.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.BUILD_FEATURE_PHONETIC"},{"category":"constant","location":"#Liblevenshtein.DEFAULT_MATCH_BATCH","page":"API and usage","text":"Default maximum number of match descriptors per native batch.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.DEFAULT_MATCH_BATCH"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.Algorithm","page":"API and usage","text":"Edit-distance algorithm.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.Algorithm"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.AutomatonLimits","page":"API and usage","text":"Explicit hard limits for standalone complete and online automata evaluation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.AutomatonLimits"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.BorrowedBatch","page":"API and usage","text":"A lexical read-only sequence of borrowed matches for one reducer callback.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.BorrowedBatch"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.BorrowedMatch","page":"API and usage","text":"A lexical zero-copy descriptor valid only during one reducer callback.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.BorrowedMatch"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.GeneralizedAutomaton","page":"API and usage","text":"An immutable native generalized-automaton configuration.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.GeneralizedAutomaton"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.GeneralizedObservation","page":"API and usage","text":"A precise observation of one generalized target prefix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.GeneralizedObservation"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.GeneralizedOnlineAutomaton","page":"API and usage","text":"An exclusive generalized online-prefix state.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.GeneralizedOnlineAutomaton"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.GeneralizedOperation","page":"API and usage","text":"An immutable runtime generalized edit-operation description.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.GeneralizedOperation"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.GeneralizedOperationSet","page":"API and usage","text":"An immutable, typed collection of generalized edit operations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.GeneralizedOperationSet"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.GeneralizedRestriction","page":"API and usage","text":"One directional source-to-target restriction for a listed generalized edit.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.GeneralizedRestriction"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.Match","page":"API and usage","text":"One independently owned fuzzy match whose term type preserves its unit domain.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.Match"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.NativeError","page":"API and usage","text":"A copied native failure with its stable status, operation, and diagnostic.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.NativeError"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.OperationApplicability","page":"API and usage","text":"Runtime generalized-operation applicability predicate.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.OperationApplicability"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.PhoneticPattern","page":"API and usage","text":"An immutable compiled phonetic-language automaton.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.PhoneticPattern"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.PhoneticRuleSet","page":"API and usage","text":"An immutable parsed or built-in phonetic rewrite-rule set.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.PhoneticRuleSet"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.PhoneticRuleSetKind","page":"API and usage","text":"Built-in phonetic rewrite-rule set.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.PhoneticRuleSetKind"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.PrefixObservations","page":"API and usage","text":"A finite exclusive stream of online-prefix observations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.PrefixObservations"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.QueryCache","page":"API and usage","text":"An exclusive bounded complete-query cache backed by native TinyLFU admission and SIEVE eviction. The object has no internal lock; use one cache per Julia task or worker when queries run in parallel.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.QueryCache"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.QueryCacheStats","page":"API and usage","text":"A copied snapshot of bounded query-cache policy and residency counters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.QueryCacheStats"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.QueryCursor","page":"API and usage","text":"An exclusive one-shot fuzzy result iterator retaining its query-start snapshot.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.QueryCursor"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.QueryOrder","page":"API and usage","text":"Lazy result ordering.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.QueryOrder"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.Status","page":"API and usage","text":"Result of a fallible native operation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.Status"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.Transducer","page":"API and usage","text":"A shareable algorithm configuration retaining a versioned dictionary provider.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.Transducer"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.UniversalAutomaton","page":"API and usage","text":"An immutable native universal-automaton configuration.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.UniversalAutomaton"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.UniversalEquivalence","page":"API and usage","text":"One directional zero-cost source-to-target universal equivalence.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.UniversalEquivalence"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.UniversalObservation","page":"API and usage","text":"A precise observation of one universal target prefix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.UniversalObservation"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.UniversalOnlineAutomaton","page":"API and usage","text":"An exclusive universal online-prefix state in one fixed unit domain.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.UniversalOnlineAutomaton"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.UniversalPolicy","page":"API and usage","text":"An immutable non-empty directional universal-equivalence policy.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.UniversalPolicy"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.UniversalVariant","page":"API and usage","text":"Universal edit-automaton variant.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.UniversalVariant"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.UnrestrictedPolicy","page":"API and usage","text":"The allocation-free universal substitution policy.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.UnrestrictedPolicy"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.WallBreakerLimits","page":"API and usage","text":"Logical matcher limits, with implementation hard ceilings; not an RSS budget.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.WallBreakerLimits"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.WallBreakerMatch","page":"API and usage","text":"Copied Unicode WallBreaker result with exact selected-algorithm distance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.WallBreakerMatch"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.WallBreakerMatcher","page":"API and usage","text":"Finite owned Unicode term matcher; this does not accept a vt.dictionary.v1 resource.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.WallBreakerMatcher"},{"category":"type","location":"#Liblevenshtein.WallBreakerPatternPiece","page":"API and usage","text":"Native splitter projection; offsets and indices are zero-based.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.WallBreakerPatternPiece"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.abi_version","page":"API and usage","text":"Return the stable native ABI generation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.abi_version"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.accepts","page":"API and usage","text":"Return whether a complete source/target pair is accepted within its configured budget.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.accepts"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.advance!","page":"API and usage","text":"Transactionally commit one target unit and return the resulting observation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.advance!"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.api_revision","page":"API and usage","text":"Return the additive native API revision.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.api_revision"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.build_features","page":"API and usage","text":"Return the compiled native feature-bit set.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.build_features"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.cache_stats","page":"API and usage","text":"Copy aggregate TinyLFU/SIEVE policy counters and current residency.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.cache_stats"},{"category":"method","location":"#Liblevenshtein.cancel!-Tuple{WallBreakerCursor}","page":"API and usage","text":"Stop iteration and discard copied pending matches; later next_batch! raises STATUS_CLOSED.\n\nThe native query has already completed when the cursor is created, so this does not interrupt matching work inside query.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.cancel!"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.clear!","page":"API and usage","text":"Drop all resident cached query results while retaining policy counters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.clear!"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.close!","page":"API and usage","text":"Deterministically release an owned native handle; repeated calls are harmless.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.close!"},{"category":"method","location":"#Liblevenshtein.damerau_distance-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"API and usage","text":"Compatibility spelling for optimal_string_alignment_distance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.damerau_distance"},{"category":"method","location":"#Liblevenshtein.distance-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"API and usage","text":"Compute Levenshtein distance, or nothing when it exceeds threshold.\n\nStrings are compared as Unicode scalars. Vector{UInt8} inputs are arbitrary bytes, while Vector{UInt64} inputs are application-defined tokens. Dense vectors cross the native boundary without a copy; other abstract vectors are materialized into contiguous storage for the duration of the call.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.distance"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.evaluate","page":"API and usage","text":"Evaluate a complete source/target pair and return its exact final observation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.evaluate"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.materialize","page":"API and usage","text":"Copy a callback-scoped borrowed match into an independently owned Match.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.materialize"},{"category":"method","location":"#Liblevenshtein.merge_and_split_distance-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"API and usage","text":"Compute distance with unit-cost one-to-two split and two-to-one merge edits.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.merge_and_split_distance"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.next_batch!","page":"API and usage","text":"Copy and settle one bounded native cursor batch.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.next_batch!"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.observation","page":"API and usage","text":"Read the last committed online-prefix observation without advancing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.observation"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.online","page":"API and usage","text":"Bind an immutable standalone automaton to one source for exclusive prefix processing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.online"},{"category":"method","location":"#Liblevenshtein.optimal_string_alignment_distance-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"API and usage","text":"Compute adjacent-transposition (optimal-string-alignment) distance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.optimal_string_alignment_distance"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.prefix_observations","page":"API and usage","text":"Create or scope a finite prefix-observation stream that closes on exhaustion or failure.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.prefix_observations"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.query","page":"API and usage","text":"Start a lazy snapshot-consistent query selected by the input's Julia type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.query"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.reduce_batches!","page":"API and usage","text":"Consume callback-scoped zero-copy batches and close the cursor.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.reduce_batches!"},{"category":"method","location":"#Liblevenshtein.reduce_batches!-Tuple{Any, Any, QueryCursor}","page":"API and usage","text":"Reduce bounded zero-copy native batches and always consume the cursor.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.reduce_batches!"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.reset_stats!","page":"API and usage","text":"Reset cache counters without changing residency or frequency state.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.reset_stats!"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.snapshot","page":"API and usage","text":"Capture an independently owned immutable transducer revision.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.snapshot"},{"category":"method","location":"#Liblevenshtein.true_damerau_distance-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"API and usage","text":"Compute unrestricted Damerau-Levenshtein distance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.true_damerau_distance"},{"category":"function","location":"#Liblevenshtein.unit_domain","page":"API and usage","text":"Return a transducer's byte, Unicode-scalar, or u64 unit domain.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Liblevenshtein.unit_domain"}]
